  "bichkek/yourte": ["An evening in a yurt", "Beshbarmak, meat and noodles eaten by hand, and the kumis handed to you at the entrance."],
  "tachkent/chorsu": ["Chorsu Bazaar", "A giant blue dome under which dried fruit, spices and bread are piled high."],
